From: Liuqin Linux Kit contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Serialize notification enable and publish initial power state

The power-supply registration event can precede charger-service readiness,
so a cable already attached before boot may not produce another physical
attach event for consumers. Serialize notification enable on the same mutex
as property requests, then publish the available supplies after the ACK.
Do not change charger limits, voltage, PD policy or USB roles.

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index b807b9c9c..490a16ca1 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -2492,9 +2492,26 @@ static void qcom_battmgr_enable_worker(struct work_struct *work)
 	};
 	int ret;
 
+	mutex_lock(&battmgr->lock);
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_request(battmgr, &req, sizeof(req));
+	mutex_unlock(&battmgr->lock);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(battmgr->dev, "failed to request power notifications\n");
+	else {
+		/* Re-publish an already-attached supply after the firmware client
+		 * is ready. Registration may have been observed while service_up
+		 * was false, and no new physical attach event is guaranteed.
+		 * Keep all charge-current/voltage policy inside the firmware.
+		 */
+		if (battmgr->bat_psy)
+			power_supply_changed(battmgr->bat_psy);
+		if (battmgr->usb_psy)
+			power_supply_changed(battmgr->usb_psy);
+		if (battmgr->ac_psy)
+			power_supply_changed(battmgr->ac_psy);
+		if (battmgr->wls_psy)
+			power_supply_changed(battmgr->wls_psy);
+	}
 }
 
 static void qcom_battmgr_pdr_notify(void *priv, int state)
